# 07 · UI and UX

## UX Objectives
- Make primary tasks easy, fast, and predictable.
- Prioritize clarity over decorative complexity.
- Design for real error, empty, loading, and offline states.

## Consistency
- Reuse established design system/components before creating new patterns.
- Keep interaction and copy conventions consistent across surfaces.
- Preserve platform expectations where users rely on them.

## Accessibility
- Meet accessibility standards relevant to the product (WCAG/platform guidance).
- Ensure keyboard/focus/screen-reader support where applicable.
- Maintain readable contrast and scalable typography.

## Responsive and Adaptive Behavior
- Support required viewport/device classes.
- Avoid hardcoded layout assumptions that break on common form factors.
- Verify behavior in dark/light themes and localization where in scope.

## Feedback and Recovery
- Provide clear success/failure feedback for user actions.
- Offer safe undo/confirmation for destructive operations.
- Error messages should tell users what they can do next.

## Validation
- Include UX acceptance criteria in feature definitions.
- Run quick usability checks for high-impact flows before release.
